window.docContents[87].resolve({"/Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols/L2-___-The-pair-is-a-system-too/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L2-___-The-pair-is-a-system-too--Synopsis--Errors-prevented":{"contents":"* Summing what does not sum: the normal-mode frequency taken as the sum of the bodies' angular frequencies. assemble fails because no Assembles instance exists (HCP.L2_ThePair#refused_frequency_assembly).* Wrong composition law: the stiffnesses of springs in series added as if the springs were in parallel (HCP.L2_ThePair#refused_series_stiffness).* Whole/part confusion: pair P's mass added to body A's mass, a quantity about the whole combined with a quantity about one of its parts (HCP.L2_ThePair#refused_whole_part).\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L2 — The pair is a system too\u0009Synopsis","header":"5.3.1.4. Errors prevented","id":"/Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols/L2-___-The-pair-is-a-system-too/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L2-___-The-pair-is-a-system-too--Synopsis--Errors-prevented"},"/Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols/L3-___-The-body-opens-up/#hcp-l3":{"contents":"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols","header":"5.4. L3 — The body opens up","id":"/Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols/L3-___-The-body-opens-up/#hcp-l3"},"/Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols/L6-___-What-must-hold/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L6-___-What-must-hold--Synopsis--Errors-prevented":{"contents":"* Unstatable scope: \"every pair\" or \"pair P\" written without a declared sort or a nominal object to quantify over (HCP.L6_Requirements#invalid_scopes).* Over-claimed coverage: a requirement about pair P counted as governing pair Q's output (HCP.L6_Requirements#scope_gap).* Ungoverned output: a model output that no requirement governs goes unreported (HCP.L6_Requirements#requirement_census).\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L6 — What must hold\u0009Synopsis","header":"5.7.1.4. Errors prevented","id":"/Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols/L6-___-What-must-hold/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L6-___-What-must-hold--Synopsis--Errors-prevented"},"/Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes/How-a-definition-reads-___-the-rendering-family/#annotation-pkc-math-config":{"contents":"A projection of an ordinary structure renders as a function applied to its receiver:\n, which is the field name stripped of the type it belongs to\nplus a spurious application. Tagging the structure makes its projections render as the qualified\nconstant  instead, with the configuration value elided.\n\n@[pkc_math_config]\nstructure AvsConfig (α : Type) where\n  two : Quantity pureNumber α\n\n\nThe type must opt in: a blanket \"drop the receiver\" rule would wreck Prod.fst and Prod.snd.\nNote what this does not do — it does not render cfg.two as 2, which would assert something\nabout a def parameter rather than report what the definition computes.\n\n* Type* What it is* AvsConfig* The AVS forward's configuration: the two-way optical-path factor 2, as a kinded quantity — the sole numeral of the model.* DemoConfig* A configuration type: one dimensionless scale factor, the demo's sole configured constant.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Using the library: annotations and generated indexes\u0009How a definition reads — the rendering family","header":"33.8.3. @[pkc_math_config]  — a configuration type","id":"/Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes/How-a-definition-reads-___-the-rendering-family/#annotation-pkc-math-config"},"/Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes/What-a-vocabulary-answers-for-___-the-coverage-censuses/#annotation-kindRelationFree":{"contents":"The declared exception to M12, on a Provenance.Contract: a boundary whose behavior is not\na measurement model — pure data movement, or the reference the theorem edges are about —\nsaid in the author's words where the census reads them.\n\n/-- No edge, on purpose. Its port is classed. -/\n@[kindRelationFree \"a data-movement boundary: its behavior is the identity on kinds, and \\\n  there is no measurement model to carry\"]\ndef dataMove : Provenance.Contract NodeId KindRef where …\n\n\nInert on a boundary some edge names. Rejected at elaboration unless the declaration is a\nProvenance.Contract and the reason is non-empty: the mark exempts a declared boundary from\na census over declared boundaries, so that is where it goes.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Using the library: annotations and generated indexes\u0009What a vocabulary answers for — the coverage censuses","header":"33.7.2. @[kindRelationFree \"…\"]  — a boundary with no measurement model","id":"/Using-the-library___-annotations-and-generated-indexes/What-a-vocabulary-answers-for-___-the-coverage-censuses/#annotation-kindRelationFree"}});